{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '39,99p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '124,166p' docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md && sed -n '1,100p' docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md\"","aggregated_output":"### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\n\nRequirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\nEvidence: [source coverage](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:6)\nand [narrative assertions](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:44).\n\nThe draft requires dispositions for source spans and separates document,\nsemantic and simulation coverage. It does not specify how to establish the\ncomplete disclosure inventory, resolve incorporated cross-references, carry\nqualifications from narrative into the affected figures, or verify that the\ncoverage process itself has not missed a note or table. Generic actor/predicate\nfields are insufficient to determine the executable meaning of exclusions,\nscope qualifications, contingent commitments and qualitative quantifiers.\n\nRequired evidence: one complete filing manifest, source-span disposition and\ncross-reference example; typed narrative records; a mapping from disclosures\nto supported constraints or explicit unresolved obligations. Preserve separate\ncoverage meanings and defined denominators. Do not score parsed pages as\nformalised financial meaning, or turn \"substantially all\" into an invented\nnumeric threshold.\n\n### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\n\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\n\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\n\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\n\nRequirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\nEvidence: [time and views](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:80)\nand [EvidenceView](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:92).\n\nStoring dates and supersession links does not specify which assertion wins a\nquery. The design needs precise rules for incomplete publication timestamps,\nconflicting available filings, selective restatements, changed accounting\nbases and calendars, and different investor-information versus system-version\nqueries. Prospective estimate changes and retrospective corrections are\ndelegated to future packages without a complete transition example.\n\nRequired evidence: a multi-date example with explicit publication, ingestion,\neconomic and reporting times, original and revised amounts, and the exact\nrecords/results returned by each supported view. Show invalid year-to-date\nsubtractions across revisions as well as a valid one. Declare unsupported\ntiming assumptions rather than silently using the latest available row.\n\n### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\n\n### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\n\nEvidence: [initial corporate scope](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/08-modules.tex:41)\nand [report production](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:209).\n\nSales, inventory, payroll, fixed assets and working capital are named, but\nrecognition, measurement and transition rules are not supplied as a coherent\nreference package. There is no complete company example joining accruals,\nsettlements, cost of sales, depreciation, closing, cash-flow classification\nand changes in equity. Consolidation, foreign-currency translation and\nrestatement have sound stated requirements but lack equivalent numerical\nspecifications. The tests for these operations mostly describe desired\nproperties without complete inputs and expected outputs.\n\nRequired repair: provide one deliberately bounded corporate profile with an\nopening state, event schedules, journal templates and all statement mappings.\nCarry it across annual and interim periods, including a correction and one\nperimeter or currency case. Every supported operation needs its assumptions,\npreconditions, state changes and expected reports; explicit exclusions are\nacceptable. A balanced financing illustration does not specify this package.\n\n### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\n\nEvidence: [proposed demonstrator](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:128),\n[ingestion](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:6),\nand [example request](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:234).\n\nThe document proposes a real company and a synthetic company but does not\ninstantiate either as a full disclosure package. There is no named filing\nset with source passages, extracted records, alternative readings, resolved\ncross-references, history constraints and resulting conditional statements.\nThe mathematical example starts after the consequential interpretation work\nhas already been supplied by hand.\n\nRequired repair: add a complete synthetic fixture whose hidden history is known\nand a bounded, named real annual/interim disclosure case. Show representative\nnotes including narrative qualifications, missing terms, a contradiction and\na revised comparative. A worked specification can be written before the\nengine exists; the gap is not simply the absence of production code.\n\n### G6. Forward economic and probability models remain interfaces\n\nEvidence: [forward equations](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:119),\n# Active checkpoint\n\nUpdated: 2 October 2026 (Asia/Hong_Kong), after multi-year source-corpus\nacceptance following the expanded-audit repair. The user directed us to do all\nfeasible internal work before costly professional review. MC35 preserves that work order.\nThe wider mission remains active; human review is not the next automatic step.\n\n## Accepted source corpus and next execution\n\nThe user's corpus-first work unit is complete at the source-acquisition layer:\n**192 of 192 target reports, 2018–2025, across nine issuers and three evidenced\naccounting families. All nine have eight consecutive complete years.**\n`target-panel-v2.json` is active and is now the collector's explicit default.\nHenkel replaces Unilever and Munich Re replaces Allianz under the reviewed\nsource-access repair; frozen v1 coverage and all original files remain under\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/snapshots/`.\n\nResume from the [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n`data/financial-report-benchmark/index.html`, `coverage.json` and\n`integrity-manifest.json`. QA 6 revalidated all 244 retained original versions;\nthe independent hash/provenance/grid/PDF checks pass, and 20 regression tests\npass. The old 12-, 157- and 159-report counts are historical. There are 738\nattempt/revalidation records, not 738 benchmark observations.\n\nThe collector checkpoints each attempt and supports `--revalidate-retained`,\n`--resolved-only`, sequential `--index-plan` capture and bounded host failures.\nOfficial HSBC and Midea archives, SAIC year pages, Ping An's published report\nfeed, SEC submissions and issuer-hosted US filing feeds have been resolved.\nDirect SEC archive downloads returned 403; issuer-hosted copies are used with\nthe regulator identity and filing dates retained. Run one acquisition writer\nat a time. The optional `--http-client curl` bounds total request time;\n`--source-host` can select a resolved alternate without retrying known failures.\nPing An's last ASBE slot was filled by an A-share report attachment on a public\nmirror; the distinct IFRS copy remains excluded from that slot. Do not reset\nthe ledger, initialise Git or promote source checks into accounting evidence.\n\nThe next internal work is task-specific literal/context/span annotation and\nCore 0 semantic/compiler implementation using the preserved source set and\nexisting fixtures. `benchmark-protocol-v1.json` and\n`annotation-record.schema.json` define the proposed tasks and exchange format;\nissuer-family roles are provisional, with no model score or gold labels.\nResolve incorporated documents, revisions and publication timing before\nhistorical forecasting. Publication dates are unverified for 136 of 192\naccepted reports; 56 have filing-date metadata. No paid review is triggered.\n\n## Current deliverable\n\n`docs/design/accounting-product-design.pdf` and its LaTeX sources are Version\n1.2, a 79-page design candidate with 11 chapters and two appendices. It contains\ncomplete Northstar annual/interim/revision/forecast cases, an Apple filing\ninventory and conditional financing stress, historical construction and solver\nlimits, corporate operations, sector examples, Core 0 contracts,\nreview/replay/adapter definitions and corpus/release protocols.\n\nThe 8 mission goals and MC01–MC34 retain their requirement and acceptance\nwording. MC35 adds the new cost/preparation requirement. Assessments identify\nevidence and residual obligations. A bounded debt semantic validator, frozen\nregistry and three accounting source dossiers supplement the design. Version\n1.2 corrects the Caterpillar note anchor and states separate reinsurance PAA\neligibility/recognition/timing; it preserves the prior calculations.\nControl files:\n\n- `MISSION_CONTROL.md`\n- `docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md`\n- `docs/plans/accounting-before-paid-review.md`\n- `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md`\n- `docs/design/review/internal-preparation-results.md`\n- `docs/design/review/internal-preparation-manifest.json`\n- `docs/plans/accounting-gap-repair-2026-10-02.md`\n- `docs/design/review/repair-plan-review-2026-10-02.md`\n- `docs/design/review/gap-repair-results-2026-10-02.md`\n- `docs/design/review/author-review.md`\n- `docs/design/review/repair-verification.json`\n- `docs/design/review/repair-execution-note.md`\n\nThe preparation manifest records the earlier Version 1.2 preparation state.\nCorpus-era controls and `fixtures/corpus-protocol.json` have since been updated;\ntheir current hashes are in `data/financial-report-benchmark/release-manifest.json`.\nThe older repair manifest identifies historical Version 1.1; neither historical\nmanifest should be treated as a current hash set for changed control files.\n`docs/design/README.md` gives reading routes and commands.\n\n## Evidence preserved\n\nThe protected original 60-page draft, controls and affected scripts are under\n`docs/design/review/pre-repair-2026-10-02/`, with 45 file hashes. Its PDF hash is\n`0b83e17e8f7906c8ea341cb6c1ef2b3082069ca59577eb0ae7d22b50c54163f0`.\nVersion 1.1 also remains protected in `pre-expert-preparation-2026-10-02/`\n(44 files), with its rendered evidence in `repair-render/version-1.1/`.\nNo old display equations or citation keys were removed; grammar/record changes\nand preserved qualifications have an author disposition.\n\nChecks: 12 original illustrations, 49 repair/reference checks and 31\ncore-contract/reference checks pass. The new semantic suite passes 78 checks\n(5 positive, 71 schema-valid negative, 2 JSON-boundary); the new accounting\ndossiers pass 17 exact/journal checks. These are bounded author evidence. The revised PDF has no serious TeX\nwarnings and received contact-sheet plus selected full-page inspection.\nThe verifier requires an author-review file and matching current-PDF render\nmanifest and tracks the external grammar input. The library contains 32\nverified paper PDFs. There are 179 individual title/metadata decisions across\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
